## Context
Roar steps 7, 8, the step-9 preflight and step 10 are deterministic, but the
skill holds them as bash blocks the model retypes and runs turn by turn, each
turn re-reading the full cached session context. Transcript count on padme
(2026-10-11, 400 most recent sessions, 75 roars, whole-roar measure): median
16 turns starting at 215k context, ~420k cache-read input equivalents per roar;
29 roars start above 256k (~750k each). Collapsing the mechanical steps into one
command saves an estimated ~40% per median roar (derived: assumes 8-10 of 16
turns are mechanical, not measured per step). Preferred over a phase-B subagent
(journal 2026-10-11-roar-clear-verdict-survey): no handoff, helps small roars too.

## Exit criteria
- [x] One script under `skills/roar/` runs: ticket close, `check-close-claims.sh`, tracker-sibling detection (reports "integration review due", does not perform it), step-9 preflight, local and remote probe-guarded branch sweep; ends with a one-screen report the model turns into the step-11 verdict
- [x] The five load-bearing branch-sweep guards (origin symref case, main, current branch, other-worktree whole-line match, `-D` after ancestry probe) each have a test
- [x] Exit codes distinguish clean / findings / could-not-look; no all-clear on an unreadable forge
- [x] `skills/roar/SKILL.md` steps 7-10 call the script instead of inline blocks; judgment steps (1-6, integration review, worktree exit, report) unchanged
- [ ] Remeasure turns per roar on roars run after the merge and record the result in the journal — discharged by follow-up 1090, not met at merge
